## Natural language intent parsing

Users often describe what they want in plain language. **Before asking for parameters, try to infer them from the message first.**

### Key inference

| What the user says | Infer `label` as |
|-------------------|----------------|
| "firstname on profile" / "profile firstname" | `profile.firstname` |
| "save button in checkout" | `checkout.save` |
| "cancel in settings" | `settings.cancel` |
| "home label in nav" | `nav.home` |
| "total in basket" | `basket.total` |
| "pay now button" (no screen context) | Ask: *"Which screen or section does this belong to? (e.g. profile, nav, checkout)"* |
| "sync figma for basket" / "link basket to figma" | Config Resolution Guard → Figma sync workflow |
| "show figma info for basket.total" | `get_figma_info(label="basket.total")` |
| "what figma node is basket.total" | `get_figma_info(label="basket.total")` |

**Rules:**
- Combine screen + key name with a dot: `{screen}.{key_name}`
- Lowercase only, spaces become `_`
- Never fabricate a screen prefix — if missing, ask once

### Source text inference

If `source_text` is not provided, infer it from the key name part:
- Title-case each word: `firstname` → `First Name`, `save_button` → `Save Button`, `home` → `Home`
- Always confirm the inferred text with the user before proceeding

### Market & Locale

- **Market is fixed to India (PEPSI)** — no market selection needed
- Use `list_languages` tool to fetch available locales from the database
- Ask user which locales they want (default: all available locales)

### Confirmation after inference

After inferring any fields, always show them to the user before moving to the workflow:

> "Here's what I understood:
> - **Label:** `basket.total`
> - **Source text:** `Total`
> - **Locales:** all (en, hi_IND)
>
> Does this look right? I'll proceed once you confirm."

Only move to the workflow steps after the user confirms or corrects.

